SSRuntime/SettingsView.swift
Closes settings and resumes the run
Captions follow their own setting, whatever the audio is set to. Important shows damage, telegraphs, detection, Lockdown, and Extraction. Every safety warning also shows on the HUD or in the world, so no audio event is its only carrier.
The Camera counter normally appears once a Camera is damaged. The ghost replays your best run on today's layout and never affects the run.
Reduced motion swaps state changes instantly instead of animating them. Reduced flash removes full-screen luminance changes. Every warning keeps its shape and caption.
Recorded on the run receipt. Settings never change the outcome of a run or its digest.
Reset to defaults
Tutorial prompts
Scales readouts. Controls never shrink below their touch target.
Mirrors the movement stick and Dodge. Pause and readouts do not move.
Always show Camera counter
Shows your best run on today's layout as a translucent silhouette.
Voice and captions
Important shows safety warnings only. All adds routine sounds. Off hides captions.
